<h1>Uni-Vishwas — Privacy and data use</h1><p>Updated 20 October 2026 · Application release 1.8.0</p>
<p>Uni-Vishwas supports resident information and society services at Uninav Heights. This notice describes the information handled by the application and how it is used.</p>
<h2>Information handled</h2><p>Account information includes flat and tower identifiers, names, account relationships and password hashes. Email addresses and profile photos may be present where provided. Features may also store complaints and attachments, poll participation, parking and vehicle details, guest entry records, gym visits and child pass names. Staff attendance records may contain names, contact numbers, photos, attendance times and location coordinates. Society and vendor directories contain contact information.</p>
<p>Resident phone-number fields and the former OTP records have been removed. This does not mean the application handles no user information.</p>
<h2>Purpose and access</h2><p>Information is used for authentication, society notices, complaints, parking, gym, attendance and the other features selected by users or managed by authorised society staff. Administrators and designated operational roles can access information required for their responsibilities. Complaint notifications may be sent to the configured society contact and to the resident's supplied email address.</p>
<h2>Security</h2><p>The application requires HTTPS, uses secure cookies, stores login passwords as one-way hashes and protects uploaded media and PHP session files using authenticated encryption. Media is delivered through authenticated application routes. Existing uploads are converted during the security upgrade or on authorised access. Database, operating-system, mail-service and hosting backup protections must also be maintained by the operator. Security depends on correct deployment and ongoing verification.</p>
<h2>Service providers</h2><p>The hosting and email providers process the information needed to operate their services. Existing QR/OCR features load libraries or language models over HTTPS from jsDelivr and the Tesseract language-data provider; those providers may receive standard connection information. OCR is performed in the user's browser. Background notifications disclose only generic update messages; sign-in is required to view application content.</p>
<h2>Android app</h2><p>The Android app shows these pages and adds phone notifications. Notifications are delivered by Google Firebase Cloud Messaging, which assigns the installed app a messaging token (a device identifier) and processes it to deliver messages; the society server does not store these tokens, and the messages contain only generic update text. The app also asks Google Play whether a newer version is available. The camera is used only when you scan a QR code or a vehicle number plate, take a photo for an upload or mark attendance; location is used only when attendance is marked; downloaded reports are saved to the phone. Notification, camera and location access can be refused or withdrawn in the phone's settings at any time.</p>
<h2>Retention and requests</h2><p>Information is retained as needed for account operation and society records. Residents can request correction, account deletion and review of associated records through the contact below. The administrator must verify the request and consider any applicable record-retention requirements. Backup retention is managed separately by the hosting operator.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2><p>For privacy or account requests, contact <a href="mailto:<?= htmlspecialchars(COMPLAINTS_INBOX,ENT_QUOTES,'UTF-8') ?>"><?= htmlspecialchars(COMPLAINTS_INBOX,ENT_QUOTES,'UTF-8') ?></a>.</p>
